5. DUPLICATE PATIENT HANDLING
==================================================

IMPORTANT BUSINESS RULE:

There should be one master patient profile for an identified patient.

Before creating a patient, the practitioner should be able to search existing patients.

If an existing patient is found:
- reuse that patient
- create a new assessment for that patient when needed

Do NOT create duplicate patient records simply because another doctor/student is conducting an assessment.

However:

DO NOT implement fuzzy matching.

DO NOT assume that:

name + date_of_birth + phone

is a guaranteed unique identity.

These fields should be used for search/filtering and duplicate prevention workflow.

Do NOT create a composite UNIQUE database constraint on name + DOB + phone unless there is an explicit existing project requirement.

